cy ordering (P5): test suites before code, foundational code before features, libraries before CLI. And P2 says to split implementation and tests into separate tasks.\n\nBut wait - the spec status is \"spec_complete\" meaning PRD, use case, and test suite exist. So the documentation is done. I need to propose code tasks.\n\nSince I can only propose 1 task and it should be implementation first (before tests per P8), I should propose the du implementation task.\n\nNow I'm realizing I need to anchor this to specific PRD requirement IDs, but I don't have the actual PRD content for du. The spec shows rel01.3-uc001-du as spec_complete with code not started, and I don't see a corresponding PRD in the orphaned list. I'm facing a constraint conflict here—I can't explore the filesystem to find the PRD, but I also need to reference specific requirement IDs to make this task concrete. about what du does: it reports disk usage of files and directories with various flags for formatting and filtering. But I shouldn't invent requirements—I need to reference the actual PRD. Looking at the constraints again, I should propose a task that references the PRD file and specific requirement IDs, even if I don't have the full content in front of me, and let the stitch agent handle reading it.\n\nSince I can only create one task and implementation should be separate from tests per the guidelines, I'll propose the du implementation task that covers the core functionality, referencing the PRD and architecture documents in required_reading.\n\nNow I'm looking at the PRD references and version discrepancies—the implementation status shows du is at rel02.0 with specs complete, but the code status indicates rel01.3. Let me figure out which PRD file corresponds to du and reconcile these versions.\n\nThe constraint about anchoring tasks to specific PRD requirement IDs is clear, but without the actual PRD content in the provided context, I can't extract those exact IDs. Since I can't use tools to loo