ions, then lay out the specific requirements for the du command implementation—covering flag parsing with both short and long forms, recursive directory traversal using lstat to handle symlinks correctly, and disk usage accumulation in 512-byte blocks as the POSIX standard dictates.\n\nThe output formatting needs to support multiple modes: standard block output, human-readable sizes, summary-only, grand totals, and depth limiting, all in tab-separated format. Error handling follows the contract of exiting cleanly on success, returning 1 on any failure, printing diagnostics to stderr, and continuing to process remaining paths when one fails.\n\nThe implementation lives in cmd/du/main.go as a standalone binary following the cmd/ package pattern, with string comparisons and output using C locale semantics for consistency.  I'll import pkg/sys for file metadata and pkg/format for size formatting if they exist on the branch, falling back to Go's standard library (os.Lstat, fmt.Sprintf) if needed to ensure the build succeeds. The acceptance criteria require the binary to compile cleanly, pass vet checks, and correctly output tab-separated block counts and paths for directories. I'm satisfied with this structure. Let me do a final check on the constraints—with 4 requirements, this is deterministic given the input, and they're fundamental to any du implementation, so they should remain consistent across runs. Now I'll write the full response.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19052,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f079595-cc06-4c10-a7e3-c4e539486082","uuid":"7eebea04-6e38-4c6a-a5b5-4ca2b0ecc29a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GuNYDpU1fv2VhLrtDnqiNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with:\n- `cmd/` — one Go package per utility\n- `pkg/sys/` — cross-platform syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness\n- `docs/` — PRDs, use cases, test suites (human-authored)\n- `magefiles/` — build orchestration (scaffolded, not a generation target)\n\n**Current state**: Specifications are complete for testutils, sys, format, ts, wc, cat, sponge, du, and ls. Generated Go code (4,586 LOC) exists at generation-merged tags but is **not present on the working branch** — the branch contains specifications only. No Go source files exist on `generation-gh-262-codegen`.\n\n**Current release scope**: Release 01.3 — \"Batch 1.3 — du specification and differential test.\" The single use case `rel01.3-uc001-du` has spec status `spec_complete` and code status `not started`.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 01.3 has one use case: `rel01.3-uc001-du`. Spec artifacts (PRD, use case, test suite) are complete. The next step is code generation. Per P2/P8, implementation comes before tests when split into separate tasks. Since `pkg/sys` and `pkg/format` may not exist on the branch, the implementation must handle their absence gracefully.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/du: Implement core disk usage traversal and output -- rel01.3-uc001-du\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the du PRD -- filename matches prd*-du.yaml)\"\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.3-uc001-du.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.3.yaml\n      - \"docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ package pattern, pkg/sys and pkg/format responsibilities, design decisions DD3 and DD6)\"\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"du utility: flag parsing, recursive directory traversal, disk usage accumulation, formatted output\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Parse all command-line flags specified in the du PRD using the Go flag package. Support both short (-X) and GNU-style long (--flag) forms as the PRD specifies.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement recursive directory traversal that stats each filesystem entry and accumulates disk usage. Default unit is 512-byte blocks per POSIX convention. Use os.Lstat (not os.Stat) to avoid following symlinks by default, unless the PRD specifies a flag that enables symlink following.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement all output formatting modes specified in the du PRD: default block output, human-readable sizes, summary, grand total, and max-depth limiting. Output format is tab-separated size and pathname, one line per entry.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement exit code contract per the du PRD: exit 0 on success, exit 1 when any error occurs (permission denied, nonexistent path). Print error diagnostics to stderr. Continue processing remaining paths when one path fails.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"cmd/du/ contains main.go as the single source file, compiling to a standalone binary. Per ARCHITECTURE.yaml cmd/ component pattern.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"All string comparisons and output use LC_ALL=C semantics. Per ARCHITECTURE.yaml design decision DD6, locale-aware collation is deferred.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"If pkg/sys/ exists on the branch, import it for file metadata (stat block-size abstraction). If pkg/format/ exists, import it for human-readable size formatting. If either package does not exist, use Go standard library equivalents (os.Lstat for metadata, fmt.Sprintf for formatting). Per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3, shared pkg/ is preferred but compilation must succeed.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/du/ exits 0 -- the binary compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/du/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Binary invoked with no flags on a directory prints tab-separated block-count and directory path to stdout, one line per subdirectory\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Binary invoked with the human-readable flag prints sizes with unit suffixes (K, M, G) instead of raw block counts\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Binary invoked with the summary flag prints only a single summary line per argument path\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Binary invoked with the grand-total flag appends a total line at the end of output\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Binary invoked on a nonexistent path writes a diagnostic to stderr and exits with code 1\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19052,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f079595-cc06-4c10-a7e3-c4e539486082","uuid":"9aaa6fc3-10cb-4eda-899d-f3dd37c25bb1"}
